With a fingerprint persona (--fingerprint, unless --disable-spoofing contains
"font"), 023 lets web content see only the fonts that ship with macOS. The
reserved fonts of FontServices.framework (PingFangUI.ttc: the system font's
Chinese, and PingFang SC, TC, HK and MO) ship with macOS too, so system-ui no
longer draws Chinese with the primary font's missing glyph. A font only the
host has that also ships with macOS under the same PostScript name (PingFang
downloaded for the host's languages) is replaced by the copy that ships with
macOS in lookups, fallback and style matching, as on a Mac without the
download. The per-script default font lists (such as ",Osaka,BIZ
UDGothic,Menlo") skip families the host only has. Without --fingerprint,
behaviour is unchanged.

